Pet Management: High-Impact CRUD Operations
Add a New Pet (Success Path)
Title: Ensure a new pet can be added to the store with valid, complete data
Scenario: Successfully add a new pet
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a POST request to /pet with valid JSON payload containing id, name, category, photoUrls, tags, and status
Then the response status code should be 200 (or 201, per REST conventions)
And the response body should contain the submitted pet data
And the pet should be retrievable by its ID

Add a New Pet (Invalid Data)
Title: Prevent creation of pets with invalid or missing required fields
Scenario: Attempt to add a pet with missing required fields
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a POST request to /pet with a JSON payload missing required fields (e.g., no name or photoUrls)
Then the response status code should be 400 (Bad Request)
And the response should indicate which fields are invalid or missing

Update an Existing Pet (Success Path)
Title: Ensure an existing pet's details can be updated
Scenario: Successfully update a pet's details
Given a pet exists in the store with a known ID
When I send a PUT request to /pet with updated JSON payload for that pet
Then the response status code should be 200
And the response body should reflect the updated pet data
And subsequent GET requests for the pet should return the updated data

Update a Non-Existent Pet
Title: Prevent updates to non-existent pets
Scenario: Attempt to update a pet that does not exist
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a PUT request to /pet with a JSON payload for a non-existent pet ID
Then the response status code should be 404 (Not Found)

Delete a Pet
Title: Ensure a pet can be deleted from the store
Scenario: Successfully delete a pet
Given a pet exists in the store with a known ID
When I send a DELETE request to /pet/{petId}
Then the response status code should be 200
And subsequent GET requests for the pet should return 404 (Not Found)

Delete a Non-Existent Pet
Title: Handling deletion requests for non-existent pets
Scenario: Attempt to delete a pet that does not exist
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a DELETE request to /pet/{petId} for a non-existent pet ID
Then the response status code should be 404 (Not Found)

Order Management: Critical Business Logic
Place an Order (Success Path)
Title: Ensure an order can be placed for an available pet
Scenario: Successfully place an order
Given a pet exists in the store and is available
When I send a POST request to /store/order with valid order details (petId, quantity, shipDate, status, complete)
Then the response status code should be 200
And the response body should contain the order details
And the order should be retrievable by its ID

Place an Order for a Non-Existent Pet
Title: Prevent orders for non-existent pets (Logical Consistency)
Scenario: Attempt to place an order for a non-existent pet
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a POST request to /store/order with a non-existent petId
Then the response status code should be 400 or 404
And the response should indicate the pet does not exist

Retrieve Order by ID
Title: Ensure an existing order can be retrieved
Scenario: Successfully retrieve an existing order
Given an order exists in the store with a known ID
When I send a GET request to /store/order/{orderId}
Then the response status code should be 200
And the response body should contain the order details

User Management: Authentication and Security
Create a User (Success Path)
Title: Ensure a new user can be created
Scenario: Successfully create a new user
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a POST request to /user with valid user details
Then the response status code should be 200
And the user should be retrievable by username

Create a User with Invalid Data
Title: Prevent creation of users with invalid data
Scenario: Attempt to create a user with invalid data
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a POST request to /user with invalid or missing required fields
Then the response status code should be 400
And the response should indicate invalid or missing fields

Security and Availability Risks
Unauthenticated Access to Sensitive Endpoints
Title: Ensure sensitive endpoints enforce authentication
Scenario: Attempt to access a sensitive endpoint without authentication
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a request to a sensitive endpoint (e.g., /user/{username}) without authentication
Then the response status code should be 401 (Unauthorized)

Excessive Data Exposure
Title: Ensure API responses do not expose unnecessary data
Scenario: Retrieve pet or user details
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a GET request to /pet/{petId} or /user/{username}
Then the response should contain only the necessary fields
And sensitive or internal fields should not be exposed

Rate Limiting and Abuse Prevention
Title: Ensure the API is protected against abuse and DoS
Scenario: Send a high volume of requests in a short time
Given the Petstore API is available
When I send a rapid sequence of identical requests to any endpoint
Then the API should enforce rate limiting
And excess requests should be rejected with status 429 (Too Many Requests)
